  "_meta": {
    "lastBuilt": "2026-07-17",
    "schemaVersion": 2,
    "purpose": "Named zones on the property. Each zone carries vertices (fractional 0-1 coords of the base image), a status (draft / confirmed / flagged), and a history log of changes. Observations and plants reference zones via the zoneId field. The browse view is itself a thinking tool — looking at the whole property from above helps Mom form mental models of where things are.",
    "coordinateSystem": "wgs84",
    "vertexOrder": "[lon, lat]  — GeoJSON order (x, y). NOT [lat, lon].",
    "schemaNotes": "v2 (2026-07-16): vertices are REAL WGS84 [lon, lat] coordinates. v1 stored fractions of the base image, which meant the record said where a zone APPEARED IN A PICTURE, not where it IS — swap the picture and every polygon moved, and the v1 base was an oblique Google Earth screenshot whose pixels can never be reconciled to a nadir map, so the v1 polygons were unsalvageable. Vertices are now independent of the basemap: a new basemap is a re-registration (update _meta.baseImage + bounds), never a redraw. Zone ids/names are preserved from v1 because plants.json and observations reference them via zoneId.",
    "baseImage": "images/property-map/base-naip-2022-01-leafoff.webp",
    "baseImageFallbackPng": "images/property-map/base-naip-2022-01-leafoff.png",
    "baseImageWidth": 1500,
    "baseImageHeight": 1500,
    "bounds": {
      "west": -84.36990044993301,
      "south": 34.54754054054054,
      "east": -84.364899550067,
      "north": 34.55165945945946
    },
    "boundsNote": "The georeference. Rendering maps each axis LINEARLY and INDEPENDENTLY against its own bound (lon->x, lat->y); the two axes do not share a degrees-per-pixel scale. Across this image the linear-vs-true-Mercator error is sub-centimetre — ~1000x below the imagery's own.",
    "baseImageSource": "USDA NAIP via Microsoft Planetary Computer",
    "baseImageLicense": "public domain (US federal work) — redistributable",
    "baseImageStacItem": "ga_m_3408430_sw_16_060_20220110",
    "baseImageCaptureDate": "2022-01-10",
    "baseImageSeason": "leaf-off",
    "accuracyHonesty": "Vertices traced off this basemap are HYPOTHESES, not measurements. NAIP's declared accuracy is +/-6 m @ 95% (~20 ft), and relief displacement at 2,959 ft makes the real budget ~15-30 ft. Good enough for the question these zones answer ('what's growing here?' -> a zone NAME); not good enough to place an individual plant. If a GPS track ever disagrees with a boundary by metres, BOTH can be right — different frames.",
    "lastBuiltAt": "2026-07-17T02:33:06.790Z"
  },
